1
00:00:01,585 --> 00:00:10,681
This walkthrough follows a single API request through BIN Intelligence: the key, the scope, the rate limit, the lookup, and the log.

2
00:00:13,394 --> 00:00:24,458
Every paid key carries permission scopes and a limit of twenty-five requests a second. The same payment is shown four ways, so you can see exactly what each kind of caller gets back.

3
00:00:26,577 --> 00:00:34,425
At volume, the pattern holds. Lookups are counted, never capped, so a merchant's checkout is never blocked by a quota.

4
00:00:36,525 --> 00:00:48,021
On the wire, the response follows the buyer's PCI level. Merchants that never store card numbers receive eight digits. Level One merchants can receive eleven, encrypted.

5
00:00:50,125 --> 00:00:58,261
When the catalogue changes, subscribers are told. A range that is retiring, or one that touches a rule, raises an event.

6
00:01:00,354 --> 00:01:10,290
And every request lands in a thirty-day log, one row per call. For an API product, that log is where support, billing and trust all begin.
